@node Top
@top MCP Terminal Docker Integration

This manual describes the @command{mcp-terminal-docker} Debian package
(version @value{VERSION}), which installs host integration for the
MCP Terminal HTTPS service running in Docker.

@menu
* Overview::                    What the package installs
* Commands::                    mcp-terminal-docker and mcp-terminal-info
* Configuration::               Host paths and JSON config
* Service::                     systemd and container lifecycle
* Sandbox::                     Worker images and project paths
* Install::                     Installing on a clean host
* Uninstall::                  remove and purge behavior
@end menu

@node Overview
@chapter Overview

The package:

@itemize @bullet
@item
pulls the matching service image from Docker Hub on install or upgrade;
@item
pulls sandbox worker images (@code{python-dev}, @code{node-dev}, @code{base-tools});
@item
creates host user @code{mcp-terminal} for log and data directory ownership;
@item
starts container @code{mcp-terminal} publishing host port 3011 by default;
@item
mounts @file{/var/run/docker.sock} so the service can spawn sandbox containers;
@item
registers @command{man} and @command{info} documentation.
@end itemize

Host log and data directories are owned by @code{mcp-terminal:mcp-terminal}.

@node Commands
@chapter Commands

@deffn {Command} mcp-terminal-docker @var{command}
@anchor{mcp-terminal-docker-command}
@end deffn

@table @asis
@item @code{start}
Start @code{mcp-terminal-docker.service}.
@item @code{stop}
Stop the service and container.
@item @code{restart}
Restart the same container instance.
@item @code{recreate}
Remove and recreate the container (after config, certificate, or bind-mount changes).
@item @code{status}
Show systemd and container status.
@item @code{info}
Same summary as @command{mcp-terminal-info}.
@end table

@deffn {Command} mcp-terminal-info
Print host integration summary (port, paths, image tag, container state).
@end deffn

See also @command{man mcp-terminal-docker}, @command{man mcp-terminal-info}, and
@command{man mcp-terminal-config} (JSON schema and field dependencies).

@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration

@strong{Service JSON} (main settings): @file{/etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json}.
Full reference: @command{man mcp-terminal-config}.

@table @file
@item /etc/default/mcp-terminal
Host Docker settings: port, paths, optional network, extra project bind mounts.
@item /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
Service configuration (conffile). Container path:
@file{/etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json}. Seed:
@file{/usr/share/mcp-terminal/term_server.json}.
@item /var/log/mcp-terminal
Application logs (owned by @code{mcp-terminal}).
@item /var/mcp-terminal
Application data and caches.
@item /etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates
TLS certificates; use absolute @file{/etc/mcp-terminal/...} paths inside JSON.
@end table

Validate before recreate:

@example
python3 -m mcp_terminal.config.config_cli validate -c /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
@end example

Key JSON sections: @code{server}, @code{registration}, @code{queue_manager},
@code{watch_dirs}, @code{terminal}, @code{code_analysis}.
Set @code{server.log_dir} to @code{/var/log/mcp-terminal} and
@code{server.host} to @code{0.0.0.0} in production.

@node Service
@chapter Service

@example
sudo systemctl start mcp-terminal-docker
sudo systemctl stop mcp-terminal-docker
sudo mcp-terminal-docker recreate
@end example

After configuration changes, run @code{mcp-terminal-docker recreate} or
@code{systemctl start mcp-terminal-docker-recreate.service}.

The container mounts the host Docker socket. Sandbox session containers are
created on the host by the service process inside the container.

@node Sandbox
@chapter Sandbox worker images and project paths

Sandbox images are listed in @file{/usr/lib/mcp-terminal/sandbox-images-spec}
(default registry @code{<docker-user>/mcp-terminal-*} on Docker Hub).

Project directories referenced in @code{watch_dirs} must exist on the host
filesystem where the Docker daemon runs. Bind-mount the same paths into the
service container using @code{MCP_TERMINAL_EXTRA_BINDS} in
@file{/etc/default/mcp-terminal}, for example:

@example
MCP_TERMINAL_EXTRA_BINDS=/home/projects:/home/projects
@end example

@node Install
@chapter Install

On a clean Debian/Ubuntu host:

@example
sudo dpkg -i mcp-terminal-docker_@value{VERSION}_amd64.deb
sudo apt -f install
mcp-terminal-info
@end example

@code{apt -f install} resolves package dependencies including @code{docker.io}.

Place TLS material under @file{/etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates/} before
first start if registration uses HTTPS.

@node Uninstall
@chapter Uninstall

@example
sudo apt remove mcp-terminal-docker
sudo apt purge mcp-terminal-docker
@end example

On @code{apt purge}, maintainer scripts stop systemd, remove the container,
and remove the saved service Docker image using @file{/usr/lib/mcp-terminal/image-spec}
and/or a saved ref under @file{/var/lib/mcp-terminal/}.

@bye
